\id BAD Deliberately malformed fixture
\ide UTF-8
\h Bad Book
\toc1 The Deliberately Malformed Book
\toc2 Bad Book
\toc3 Bad
\mt1 Bad Book
\c 1
\p
\v 1 This verse opens a footnote \f + \ft that is never closed.
\v 2 This verse number is duplicated below.
\v 2 The duplicate.
\v This verse marker carries no number at all.
\v 4 The last verse skips a number and ends the book.
\c 2
\s1 Line by line: verses run together
\p
\v 1 Several verses \v 2 run together \v 3 on one line, as some files have them.
\v 4
\v 5
\s1 Poetry inside verses
\q1
\v 6 A verse that is a poem,
\q2 its second line indented,
\q1 and a third line back out.
\m \v 7 A verse that starts flush \q2 and breaks into poetry halfway through the line.
\p
\v 8 A long verse that goes on for a while so that it wraps onto a second line in the editor, to show where the wrapped text sits under the verse number and its first word.
\v 9
\v 10 The last verse, after an empty one.
\v 11 A verse with a paragraph break \p in the middle of it.
